-- title:
--   Chart dictionary for J+(ℓ) under maximal growth
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$ and $m$ with $m \ge 1$, a field $k$, and an ideal $J$ of $S = k[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ (written as `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) k`) that is assumed to be generated by a set of forms all of degree $m$. Let $\iota_k : Z_k \to \operatorname{Proj} S$ be a closed immersion of schemes satisfying the chart dictionary for $J$: for every $d \ge m$ and every $F$ homogeneous of degree $d$, one has $F \in J$ if and only if, for each $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$, the pullback along $\iota_k$ of the section of the structure sheaf over the basic open set $D_+(x_i)$ determined by the homogeneous localisation $F/x_i^{d}$ vanishes. Let $a : \{0,\dots,n\} \to k$, put $\ell = \sum_j a_j x_j$, and let $J'$ be the ideal generated by the degree-$m$ forms lying in $J + (\ell)$. Assume $J'$ has maximal growth at $m$, i.e. $\dim_k$ of the degree-$(m+1)$ graded piece of $S/J'$ equals [`Nat.macaulayPow m`](def/Nat_MacaulayPow.html#L7) applied to $\dim_k$ of its degree-$m$ piece, where the graded pieces are the degree-$d$ forms modulo those belonging to the ideal. The conclusion is: for every ideal sheaf datum $\mathcal I_\ell$ on $\operatorname{Proj} S$ whose ideal on each chart $D_+(x_i)$ is spanned by the sections $G/x_i^{d}$ with $G$ homogeneous of degree $d$ and $G \in (\ell)$, and for every closed immersion $\iota' : Z' \to \operatorname{Proj} S$ with $\ker \iota' = \ker \iota_k \sqcup \mathcal I_\ell$, the same chart dictionary holds for $J'$ and $\iota'$: for all $d \ge m$ and all $F$ homogeneous of degree $d$, $F \in J'$ if and only if the pullback along $\iota'$ of the section $F/x_i^{d}$ over $D_+(x_i)$ vanishes for every $i$.
--
--   This is the hyperplane-restriction step in the Gotzmann-style analysis of graded ideals of maximal growth: it identifies the ideal generated by the degree-$m$ forms of $J + (\ell)$ with the ideal of sections vanishing on the scheme-theoretic intersection $Z \cap V(\ell)$ in all degrees $\ge m$. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_linearForm_section_maximal_growth`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_linearForm_section_maximal_growth) in the construction of the Hilbert functor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_ProjSpace_mem_span_sup_linearForm_iff_forall_app_eq_zero_of_maximal_growth.lean

